2026-09-06T00:00Z claude note Fable 5.1 deep-QA pass found three sibling gaps, folded into this ticket's scope: `unsupported-pack`/`missing-source` documents sit in the coverage denominator but are never candidates and never counted as failures, so coverage can never reach 100% with no explanation shown; `host.observed()` throwing on an already-persisted pack counts a success as a failure and blacklists it for the session (a false negative in the opposite direction from the two gaps already described above); `state.cacheWarning` is set but never rendered anywhere, so cache-write failures are invisible even though the data exists.
